WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.424 --> 00:00:19.196
On a dark winter's day, a little girl sat in a cab with her father.

2
00:00:20.277 --> 00:00:23.499
She stared out the window as the cab drove through foggy London.

3
00:00:25.581 --> 00:00:29.004
Sara Crewe was only seven, but she seemed much older.

4
00:00:30.076 --> 00:00:32.057
She was always dreaming and thinking.

5
00:00:33.257 --> 00:00:36.658
At that moment she was thinking about her long trip from India.

6
00:00:38.398 --> 00:00:40.559
She had just arrived in London with her father.

7
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.661
It felt strange to travel from a hot, sunny place and arrive in a cold, dark one.

8
00:00:51.062 --> 00:00:53.883
Soon the cab stopped in front of a big brick house.

9
00:00:55.063 --> 00:01:00.281
A brass sign on the front door said: "Miss Minchin's Boarding School for Young Ladies."

10
00:01:00.301 --> 00:01:03.962
"Papa, is this the place?"

11
00:01:04.522 --> 00:01:05.402
Sara whispered.

12
00:01:05.422 --> 00:01:08.123
"Yes," he replied.

13
00:01:08.143 --> 00:01:10.144
"We have reached it at last."

14
00:01:11.964 --> 00:01:14.325
Sara's mother had died when Sara was born.

15
00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:17.726
Sara's father was an officer in the British army.

16
00:01:18.786 --> 00:01:22.867
He was very rich and handsome and gave Sara whatever she wanted.

17
00:01:24.107 --> 00:01:26.228
Sara had lots of toys and clothes.

18
00:01:26.928 --> 00:01:28.690
Servants took care of all her needs.

19
00:01:30.111 --> 00:01:32.334
In India she'd had only one worry.

20
00:01:33.275 --> 00:01:36.258
Her father believed that the climate in India wasn't healthy.

21
00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:39.801
So one day he would send her to school in England.

22
00:01:40.622 --> 00:01:41.923
And now that day had come.

23
00:01:44.086 --> 00:01:46.228
Captain Crewe knocked on the door of the school.

24
00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.092
A servant answered and led them inside.

25
00:01:53.964 --> 00:01:57.746
Sara looked around at the ugly sitting room with its heavy wooden furniture.

26
00:01:57.766 --> 00:02:02.688
"I don't like it here, Papa," she said.

27
00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:06.569
"But soldiers probably don't like going into battle either."

28
00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:08.850
Captain Crewe laughed.

29
00:02:10.251 --> 00:02:12.812
"Oh, Sara, you say such wonderful things.

30
00:02:13.392 --> 00:02:14.632
What will I do without you?"

31
00:02:16.093 --> 00:02:17.954
He swept her into his arms for a hug.

32
00:02:19.774 --> 00:02:23.256
A moment later the headmistress, Miss Minchin, entered the room.

33
00:02:24.468 --> 00:02:28.770
The headmistress had large fishy eyes and a large fishy smile.

34
00:02:30.031 --> 00:02:34.794
Sara thought the woman looked just like her school: tall, dull, ugly.

35
00:02:35.894 --> 00:02:38.155
Miss Minchin knew that Captain Crewe was rich.

36
00:02:40.317 --> 00:02:42.618
She tried to please him by praising Sara.

37
00:02:42.638 --> 00:02:45.499
"What a beautiful child!"

38
00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.420
the headmistress exclaimed.

39
00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.982
"But I'm not beautiful!"

40
00:02:50.482 --> 00:02:51.142
Sara thought.

41
00:02:51.162 --> 00:02:53.704
"Miss Minchin is making that up."

42
00:02:55.292 --> 00:02:59.495
Sara stood quietly near her father while he and the headmistress talked.

43
00:03:00.576 --> 00:03:05.099
Because Sara's father was very rich, Sara would have many nice things at school.

44
00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:10.123
There would be a pretty bedroom and sitting room, and a pony and carriage.

45
00:03:11.383 --> 00:03:12.424
A maid would help her.

46
00:03:13.665 --> 00:03:17.288
"Sara reads too much," Captain Crewe told the headmistress.

47
00:03:17.308 --> 00:03:20.450
"Make sure she goes outside.

48
00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.352
She should ride her pony or buy some new dolls."

49
00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:25.768
"Oh, Papa!"

50
00:03:26.228 --> 00:03:26.949
said Sara.

51
00:03:26.969 --> 00:03:29.389
"I don't need a lot of new dolls.

52
00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.170
I only need Emily."

53
00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:33.811
"Who's Emily?"

54
00:03:34.311 --> 00:03:35.291
asked Miss Minchin.

55
00:03:35.311 --> 00:03:40.273
"Tell her, Sara," Captain Crewe said, smiling.

56
00:03:40.293 --> 00:03:46.114
"She's a special doll that Papa is going to buy for me," said Sara.

57
00:03:46.134 --> 00:03:49.895
"She'll be my friend when Papa is in India.

58
00:03:50.395 --> 00:03:51.776
I'll talk to her about him."

59
00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.782
Miss Minchin's large fishy smile grew wider.

60
00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:58.944
"What an unusual child!"

61
00:03:59.464 --> 00:04:00.705
she exclaimed loudly.

62
00:04:00.725 --> 00:04:03.706
"She's such a darling girl!"

63
00:04:03.727 --> 00:04:06.808
"Yes," said Captain Crewe.

64
00:04:07.569 --> 00:04:08.769
He pulled Sara close.

65
00:04:08.789 --> 00:04:11.771
"She is truly a darling girl.

66
00:04:12.191 --> 00:04:14.913
Please take very good care of her for me, Miss Minchin."

67
00:04:14.933 --> 00:04:19.656
"Oh, I will," the headmistress promised.

68
00:04:21.036 --> 00:04:24.119
Sara stayed with her father at his hotel for several days.

69
00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:31.605
He bought her all kinds of expensive clothes—velvet dresses, fur coats, silk stockings.

70
00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:37.050
They searched many toy shops looking for Emily but couldn't find her.

71
00:04:41.313 --> 00:04:45.477
has to be a doll who can listen to me, Papa," explained Sara.

72
00:04:45.497 --> 00:04:48.780
"Most dolls don't really seem to hear."

73
00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:56.243
So they looked at big dolls and little ones, at dolls with black eyes and dolls with blue

74
00:04:56.384 --> 00:05:01.907
ones. They looked at dolls with brown curls and golden braids, dolls in all kinds of clothing.

75
00:05:03.809 --> 00:05:05.390
But none of them was quite right.

76
00:05:07.231 --> 00:05:12.334
Then one day Sara spotted a doll with golden-brown hair and an intelligent expression.

77
00:05:12.354 --> 00:05:14.276
"Look, Papa!

78
00:05:14.816 --> 00:05:15.696
There's Emily!"

79
00:05:16.237 --> 00:05:16.817
she cried.

80
00:05:18.678 --> 00:05:20.600
They went into the shop and bought the doll.

81
00:05:25.342 --> 00:05:28.983
Then they went to a dressmaker to order a grand wardrobe for Emily.

82
00:05:30.004 --> 00:05:32.925
Finally the day came when Captain Crewe had to leave.

83
00:05:34.025 --> 00:05:35.826
He and Sara were very sad.

84
00:05:38.487 --> 00:05:41.068
From her window Sara watched him get into a cab.

85
00:05:43.349 --> 00:05:44.630
Emily was by her side.

86
00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:52.380
Miss Minchin sent her sister, Miss Amelia, to check on Sara.

87
00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:53.780
"Why is this door locked?"

88
00:05:54.281 --> 00:05:55.301
asked Miss Amelia.

89
00:05:55.321 --> 00:06:00.222
"I want to be alone, please," said Sara softly.

90
00:06:03.843 --> 00:06:08.084
Miss Amelia went downstairs and told Miss Minchin about how Sara was acting.

91
00:06:08.104 --> 00:06:12.786
"I've never seen such an odd child," said Miss Amelia.

92
00:06:12.806 --> 00:06:17.867
"She has locked herself in her room, but she's not making any noise at all."

93
00:06:17.887 --> 00:06:22.401
"She's very spoiled," snapped Miss Minchin.

94
00:06:22.421 --> 00:06:25.704
"I'm surprised she isn't kicking and screaming.

95
00:06:26.104 --> 00:06:28.847
All those new clothes are absolutely ridiculous.

96
00:06:29.307 --> 00:06:31.990
Her father treats her like a little princess!"
